<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Amoaful</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1874</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-ashanti-war">Third Anglo-Ashanti War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Amoaful was fought on 31 January 1874 in the forest south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>, when a British expedition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garnet-wolseley">Sir Garnet Wolseley</a> defeated a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> army. The British advanced in a square through dense bush, using artillery and rockets, and the victory opened the road to Kumasi, which they occupied and burned days later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-amoaful.jpg" alt="Battle of Amoaful" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archibald Forbes, Arthur Griffiths and others. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Amoaful.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
